  "issue": {
    "headline": "A water system under federal oversight, and a contracting record that is public",
    "body": "Jackson's water system has been under federal oversight, which produced something unusual: a court-supervised paper trail running alongside the City's own procurement. The Mississippi Public Records Act gives a resident seven working days and a free appeal to the Ethics Commission — the strongest citizen remedy of the three states this Foundation works in, and almost nobody uses it.",
    "record": "Water system contracts and change orders, the interim manager's filed reports, and Council appropriations tied to each."
  },
